WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.005
AutoValue AI: A working prototype for historical 2023 U.S. asking-price estimates. Recorded against the local API.

2
00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:11.251
Enter a vehicle: Select a 2020 Toyota Camry with 48,000 miles and a 90% prediction interval.

3
00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:19.981
Estimate with RF05: The API returns a price estimate and a calibrated range. These are historical asking prices.

4
00:00:19.981 --> 00:00:29.288
Compare interval coverage: Choose 95% coverage: the interval widens while the point estimate stays the same.

5
00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:38.630
Try another vehicle: Estimate a certified 2021 Honda CR-V with 31,000 miles, using 90% coverage.

6
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:45.843
Review saved estimates: The API saves these requests in browser-scoped SQLite history. Three estimates are now listed.

7
00:00:45.843 --> 00:00:51.911
Inspect the model: The engineering view identifies the frozen RF05 model and checks that its serving artifacts are ready.

8
00:00:51.911 --> 00:01:00.139
Read the holdout results: On 27,589 held-out observations, mean absolute error is $10,575. The model has material limitations.

9
00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:08.360
Check interval calibration: The nominal 90% interval reached 89.10% empirical coverage. Wider intervals carry a cost in precision.

10
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:16.587
Follow the architecture: RF05 serves the estimate. River learning and external-source experiments run in separate paths.

11
00:01:16.587 --> 00:01:23.807
Review experiment decisions: The experiment log records accepted, rejected, and research-only results.

12
00:01:23.807 --> 00:01:37.001
Replay a synthetic shift: Replay 600 simulated mileage-shift events. This shows recorded research results, separate from the serving model.
